Glimwick crouched in the damp undergrowth of Stranglethorn Vale, adjusting his robes while his Succubus, Vexthra, hovered impatiently. "Keep your voice down," he hissed. "That troll camp has exactly the necklaces I need." Vexthra pouted, cracking her whip. "And if they don't? I get so bored, master." Glimwick sent a shadow bolt into the nearest brute. Chaos erupted. Vexthra seduced a berserker mid-charge, turning his roar into a dopey smile while Glimwick cursed the rest. It was going perfectly—until Vexthra's spell broke. The troll instantly one-shot the gnome with a crushing blow. Glimwick woke at the spirit healer, sighing. "Should've brought the Voidwalker."

**Answer:**
The Succubus's *Seduction* ability is a crowd-control spell that requires the demon to channel it. Because Seduction is so useful for controlling dangerous mobs, warlocks constantly leave the Succubas on defensive/assist, where she immediately casts it. However, Seduction breaks on any damage, and in chaotic questing, it frequently breaks early. This causes the Succubus to stand idle, doing zero DPS while waiting to re-cast Seduction, making her seem far less common/efficient than she actually is if managed properly. [end of text]


